{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1073608-house-of-glass-and-ivory-chronicle-introduction-draft-3","id":1073608,"title":"[House of Glass and Ivory] Chronicle introduction draft #3","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-05T00:31:53-07:00","id":1073608,"title":"[House of Glass and Ivory] Chronicle introduction draft #3","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">House of Glass and Ivory</span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This is the third draft for the intro of my next Chronicles of Darkness game. I would appreciate it if you took the time to read through it and provide some constructive criticism. Online recruitment starts in August 2017.</span></span><br /> <br /> This is a game about ruling London, the largest city in the 19th century, amidst the industrial revolution and social upheaval. This is a game about Kindred believing in democracy, tyranny and various religious systems all struggling to rule a Domain in a city that\u2019s changing and growing larger faster than ever before in recorded history.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Theme: Party Time!</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The meat of the game is about a series of Kindred parties. Some are private, while others are open for anyone who wishes to attend. Kindred need common places where they can together to resolve their issues and also relax - this is why Elysiums are so important. Hurtful shouts, soothing words, suspicious whispers, threatening sibilant hisses are all part of the Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mood: Greed Eats at the Soul</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Regardless of playing slowly and methodically or quickly and intuitively, a vampire\u2019s Humanity is in jeopardy every time he acts selfishly without considering others. Yet, the very existence of a vampire is dependent on selfish acts, which hurt others. It is a balancing act, which every vampire needs to solve for themselves. With great power and influence come many opportunities, but at what cost? With a more conservative road a vampire\u2019s choices are usually much more limited, but on the other hand his Humanity is safer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Backdrop: Betrayal, Insanity &amp; Mysticism</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The time for Prince Haddon and his pet Bishop Broughton has come to an end. The Prince has sold the idea of a united and strong First and Second Estate to the entire Domain. Except it is a lie that\u2019s choking everyone towards a Final Death. It took a lot of digging around, but the Ancillae of the city finally found out why Prince Haddon has been so interested in Westminster and the Borough: both of these locations are full of ley lines and he is a fully indoctrinated Mason of the Architects of the Monolith.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Ancillae only managed to find a single piece of paper with some sketches and mystic symbols on it, but it was enough. Using Spirit\u2019s Touch they found out that the paper belonged to Prince Haddon and that it was used as part of a ritual to cast a spell of some sort. They then started pushing for Feeding rights in Westminster, because it is prime real estate for foreigners and traders across the entire world, so also a good place to Feed on all sorts of foreigners and their associates - delicacies of the world. Instead of giving a fair share of Westminster Prince Haddon simply informed the Ancillae that the area was also infested with foreign hunters and other supernatural beings, and that any Feeding rights would have to postponed until the area was safe from conflicts that might end up in Final Death or worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> With the Kine building larger and larger machines that feed their material needs the Kindred of London were still on a medieval diet, which was starting to chafe at almost everyone else except maybe the Dragons, but those monsters were probably secretly poaching Kine anyhow without anyone having the nerve to call them out on it. With an increasing number of neonates howling for Vitae the Ancillae were left without any real answers other than the Prince\u2019s draconian orders to stay within the safety of Piccadilly, Summerstown and Pentonville - all very safe and even beautiful upper class and middle class boroughs that would never fall to the vile scum poaching and living on the outskirts of civilized Kindred society. The Ancillae noticed that they had also been systematically sidelined from their former roles when it came to matters related even tangentially with the Prince. He didn\u2019t interfere with the covenants. However, when it came to matters that were within the purview of the Domain the Prince was becoming obsessively hands on with everything. It didn\u2019t seem to matter whether it was one of the Masters of Elysium, Herald or Sheriff itself the tasks were being micromanaged or even completely handled by the Prince himself. To the point where he seemed to be grabbing as much power and influence within the Domain as possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> The final straw that broke the situation was a neonate who killed an Ancilla\u2019s favorite ghoul and then hid behind the name of the Prince. The Prince simply didn\u2019t seem all that impressed that the murder of an important ghoul should warrant any serious reprimand when the neonate in question was more precious to the Prince. After that the Prince started making changes that affected the Feeding rights of the Ancillae directly. Complaints to Bishop Lawrence fell on deaf ears. All was well and the Domain was simply going through a dry spell, which would soon be ended. The scriptures spoke of many such times throughout the history of London\u2019s Domain and Ancillae should simply be more patient. It seemed like Prince Haddon and Bishop Lawrence had turned their backs on the Ancillae, so the only viable strategy forward was to break the alliance that the two Elders had forged between them. It was then that the scrap of paper was brought back into the discussion. Maybe the Ancillae could make a case that the Prince was a member of the Architects of the Monolith? That whole bloodline was vehemently hated by most Sanctified. It could destroy the Prince and weaken the Bishop in the process.<br /> <br /> <br /> The ancillae went through with their plans by first contacting and strategizing with the Carthian Movement. They had been sitting tight in East-London just waiting for an opportunity to strike at the rich West-London. Only to be contacted by half a dozen ancillae who were ready to roll out the red carpet. Details about the defenses that The ancillae even brought a promise of Cruak to support of the coming assault. Neutralizing the Prince was part of the deal, so that the Carthians could kill him. The second part of the plan was to send a ghoul to deliver the scrap of paper that the ancillae had gathered before. Knowing that the Bishop is a Mekhet the ancillae hoped that he would use the Spirit\u2019s Touch to find out the truth about Prince Haddon. To make sure that this would happen they instructed the ghoul to push the issue - all the way to his own death if necessary. The ghoul did end up dying, but he delivered the message.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Story arch</b><br /> <br /> Prologue: Unlife under a Megalomaniac Prince<br /> <br /> Chapter 1: Invasion of the Carthian Movement<br /> <br /> Chapter 2: Carthian Rule<br /> <br /> Chapter 3: Inside a Failing Experiment<br /> <br /> Epilogue: Rise of a new Invictus Prince or Carthian Tyrant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T19:25:36-07:00","id":1074463,"title":"","content":"That's some interesting game right there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}